  "question": {
    "text": "The ionization constant of benzoic acid is <math><mn>6.46</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub></math> for silver benzoic is <math><mn>2.5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></math> . How many times is silver benzoate more soluble in a buffer of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.19</mn></math> compared to its solubility in pure water?"
  },
