  "solution": {
    "text": "Suppose S is the molar solubility of silver benzoate in water, then<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>⇌</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />So <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2.5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math> M<br />If the solubility of salt of weak acid of ionization constant <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></msub></math> is S, then <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></msub></math> and S' are related to each other at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.19</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />So <math><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6.46</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∵</mo><mtext>&nbsp;&nbsp;pH</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3.19</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">′</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">′</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6.46</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6.46</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6.46</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">′</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>7.106</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6.46</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2.75</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.658</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math><br />So the ratio of <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">′</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.658</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3.32</mn></math><br />Silver benzoate is 3.32 times more soluble in buffer of pH = 3.19 than in pure water."
  }
